# SounanShaders 遭難 ―SOUNAN― - option labels (English)
profile.LOW=Low
profile.MEDIUM=Medium
profile.HIGH=High
profile.ULTRA=Ultra
profile.comment=Quality preset. Medium is tuned for 60 fps on a mid-range GPU at 1080p. Low drops the light shafts and the beam shadows; High and Ultra sharpen shadows and smooth the fog.

screen.FLASHLIGHT=Flashlight
screen.FLASHLIGHT.comment=The beam of the flashlight, the phone light and the camera's infrared.
screen.ATMOSPHERE=Fog & Air
screen.ATMOSPHERE.comment=The drifting mist, moonlight shafts through the cedar canopy.
screen.FEAR=Fear
screen.FEAR.comment=What your heart rate and the nearness of danger do to the picture.
screen.LIGHTING=Moon & Shadow
screen.LIGHTING.comment=Moon shadows of the canopy and the wind in the trees.
screen.POST=Image
screen.POST.comment=Film grain, vignette, chromatic aberration and bloom.

option.FLASH_REDUCTION=Flash Reduction
option.FLASH_REDUCTION.comment=For photosensitive players: calmer flashlight flicker and battery stutter, no heartbeat-pulsing vignette, no breathing image, no camera interference.
option.BRIGHTNESS=Brightness
option.BRIGHTNESS.comment=Overall brightness. Raise it if you cannot see anything (the horror gets a little weaker).

option.BEAM_STRENGTH=Beam Brightness
option.BEAM_STRENGTH.comment=How brightly the flashlight and the phone light light the world.
option.BEAM_FOG=Visible Beam
option.BEAM_FOG.comment=How strongly the beam glows in the fog and dust. 0 turns the visible cone off.
option.BEAM_SAMPLES=Beam Quality
option.BEAM_SAMPLES.comment=Samples per pixel for the visible beam. More is smoother but slower.
option.BEAM_SHADOWS=Beam Shadows
option.BEAM_SHADOWS.comment=Trunks and rocks throw thin shadows in the flashlight beam (screen space).
option.LENS_COOKIE=Reflector Rings
option.LENS_COOKIE.comment=The faint rings and smudges a real flashlight reflector and lens put into the beam.
option.DUST_MOTES=Dust in the Beam
option.DUST_MOTES.comment=Specks of dust (and droplets in the forest) floating in the beam.

option.FOG_DENSITY=Fog Density
option.FOG_DENSITY.comment=How thick the mist on the mountain is. Lower it to see further.
option.FOG_NOISE=Drifting Mist
option.FOG_NOISE.comment=The fog is uneven and drifts down the mountain in slow wisps. Off: smooth fog (faster).
option.VOLUMETRIC_FOG=Moonlight Shafts
option.VOLUMETRIC_FOG.comment=Moonlight falling through gaps in the canopy, scattered in the ground fog. Turn off if it is too slow.
option.VOLUMETRIC_SAMPLES=Fog Quality
option.VOLUMETRIC_SAMPLES.comment=Samples per pixel for the fog and the light shafts. More is smoother but slower.

option.FEAR_EFFECTS=Fear Effects
option.FEAR_EFFECTS.comment=Strength of the heartbeat vignette, tunnel vision, colour fringes, breathing image and double vision.
option.PAREIDOLIA=Faces in the Dark
option.PAREIDOLIA.comment=At very high fear, something like faces seems to form in the darkness at the edge of your vision.

option.SHADOWS=Shadows
option.SHADOWS.comment=Shadows cast by the moon (by the sun in the overworld).
option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow Resolution
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=Higher gives finer canopy shadows and light shafts but is slower.
option.shadowDistance=Shadow Distance
option.shadowDistance.comment=How far the moon shadows reach. The fog hides the far forest anyway.
option.SHADOW_FILTER=Shadow Quality
option.SHADOW_FILTER.comment=Number of samples that soften the shadow edges.
value.SHADOW_FILTER.1=Low (4)
value.SHADOW_FILTER.2=Medium (8)
value.SHADOW_FILTER.3=High (12)
option.WAVING_PLANTS=Wind in the Trees
option.WAVING_PLANTS.comment=The canopy sways in slow gusts (the moonlight patches move with it); ferns and grass stir.

option.FILM_GRAIN=Film Grain
option.FILM_GRAIN.comment=Grain noise. On the mountain it grows stronger with fear and danger.
option.VIGNETTE=Vignette
option.VIGNETTE.comment=Darkens the corners. On the mountain it closes in with fear and beats with your heart.
option.CHROMATIC_ABERRATION=Chromatic Aberration
option.CHROMATIC_ABERRATION.comment=Colour fringes at the edges. Stronger at high fear, in danger and through the camera.
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH=Bloom
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH.comment=Soft glow of lamps, flames, the flare, eyes in the beam and the moon.
